      "message": "Subtracting global headers from arch headers seems correct for include-sets, but I\u0027m not sure the same is true for include/exclude sets. I\u0027m especially concerned with cases where there\u0027s overlap between the includes of set A and the excludes of set B. Maybe this ends up eventually doing the \"correct\" thing -- I\u0027m not exactly familiar enough with the code to be certain. But I think this indicates we should inspect this a bit more deeply and/or document this a bit more heavily.\n\nExample:\n\nGlobal:\n    Include: A\n    Exclude: X\nArch:\n    Include: X\n\nWhat\u0027s the appropriate arch-specific behavior? Include X, or not?",
